From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eduardo Martins <eduardo@martins.ws>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 00:20:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8015-d221: Set the Wi-Fi board type

brcmfmac names Apple firmware after the board type the device tree
carries ("apple,<board>"); without it the driver only requests the bare
brcmfmac4357-pcie.bin, which does not exist, and the dongle setup fails
with -ENOENT.

The D221's BCM4357 ships the "herculesk" images, the same name the
device's firmware recipe in Orchard uses.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015-d221.dts | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015-d221.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015-d221.dts
index c2c8486..9a1f3d2 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015-d221.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015-d221.dts
@@ -38,3 +38,7 @@ &port03 {
 		vdd-supply = <&wlan_vdd>;
 	};
 };
+
+&wifi0 {
+	brcm,board-type = "apple,herculesk";
+};
-- 
2.35.1